# Line endings.
#
# Only one rule, and only for one reason: cmd.exe is the only consumer in this
# repository that cares. It reads a .bat file by byte offset while it executes
# it, and its handling of LF-only files is unreliable around exactly the two
# constructs cleanup-stale-files.bat is built from — multi-line `if (...)`
# blocks and `for %%F in (...) do (...)` loops. A batch file that misparses is
# a batch file that does not delete the forty-five stale files it exists to
# delete, and the failure is silent: the window closes and the folder looks
# fine.
#
# `text` normalises to LF inside the repository, `eol=crlf` writes CRLF into
# the working tree on checkout. So the stored bytes stay diffable and the file
# on a Windows disk is always the form cmd.exe parses reliably, no matter which
# machine or editor produced it.
#
# Deliberately narrow. `* text=auto` would renormalise every file in the
# project, which on a repository this size is a diff nobody can read and a
# whole class of risk taken on to solve a problem that only exists in two
# files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
